# Day 18 - HTML Structure and Spacing

## 📚 Learning Objectives

* Learned the structure of an HTML document.
* Learned the difference between head and body.
* Learned how to add spacing using margins.

## HTML Structure

```text
html
│
├── head
│
└── body
```

### Head

Contains information about the webpage.

Examples:

* title
* meta
* style

### Body

Contains visible content.

Examples:

* h1
* p
* a

## New CSS Properties

### Margin

```css
margin: 40px;
```

Adds space around elements.

### Margin Top

```css
margin-top: 20px;
```

Adds space above an element.

### Margin Bottom

```css
margin-bottom: 20px;
```

Adds space below an element.

## Practical Work

* Added spacing to the webpage.
* Improved layout appearance.

## Key Takeaways

* head stores page information.
* body stores visible content.
* margin controls spacing and layout.
